<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo Telecom in $200 mln Ukraine deal.</title>
<headline>Daewoo Telecom in $200 mln Ukraine deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daewoo Telecom Ltd, a unit of the Daewoo Group, said on Wednesday it has won a $200 million order to export 1.3 million lines of digital switching system to Ukraine.  </p>
<p>A spokesman said Daewoo will provide 130,000 lines of TDX (time division exchange) a year over the next 10 years under the contract with Ukraine's state-run Ukur Telecom.</p>
<p>He said the electronics phone exchange system would be exported on a turn-key basis.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
